  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Evening Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    24 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good evening Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,211.25/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,187.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MASTERS</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TSL</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MAINLAND</td>\n                <td>₦1,213.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SOBAZ</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,679.38/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Diesel Supply Crisis Deepens as Refining Capacity Falls\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The global diesel market is facing a tightening supply crisis that could persist for months. Diesel prices have risen by about 70% from pre-war levels. Diesel has also recently become more expensive than jet fuel in Europe. The combined impact of disruptions in the Middle East and Russia has tightened the international diesel market.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/diesel-supply-crisis-deepens-as-refining-capacity-falls\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NUPRC Gives 31 Oil Block Winners 60 Days to Pay Bonuses\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian Upstream Petroleum Regulatory Commission (NUPRC) has given 31 companies that won 37 oil and gas blocks in the 2025 Licensing Round 60 days to complete their signature bonus payments. The 37 blocks span Nigeria’s Niger Delta onshore, shallow-water and deep-offshore areas, as well as frontier basins.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nuprc-gives-31-oil-block-winners-60-days-to-pay-bonuses\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Crude Falls 2% as US Prepares Fresh Iran Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was down 1.81% at $92.68 per barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) declined 1.93% to $85.38. The pullback followed gains of more than 5% in both contracts last week, driven largely by stalled US-Iran peace talks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-crude-falls-2-as-us-prepares-fresh-iran-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Tinubu vs Atiku: Key Arguments on Fuel Subsidy Removal\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The removal of petrol subsidy by President Bola Ahmed Tinubu in May 2023 remains one of Nigeria’s most contested economic policies. Arguments continue over its impact on government finances, petrol prices, businesses and households. Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has advocated an alternative approach centred on domestic refining and targeted government support.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/tinubu-vs-atiku-key-arguments-on-fuel-subsidy-removal\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iraq Targets 10 Million Bpd as OPEC Quota and Hormuz Crisis Limit Growth\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iraq is targeting a major expansion of its oil production over the next six years. Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi said Friday that Baghdad wants to raise crude output to between 8 million and 10 million barrels per day. The proposed increase would require Iraq to secure greater room to produce.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iraq-targets-10-million-bpd-as-opec-quota-and-hormuz-crisis-limit-growth\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
